# `actuarial::life_contingencies::gompertz_force`

Evaluates the Gompertz force of mortality at ages.

## Signature

```cpp
pluss::Series actuarial::life_contingencies::gompertz_force(const pluss::Series &attained_ages, double b, double c);
```

## What It Does

Returns {math}`\mu_x=b\,c^{x}` at each age: a force that grows by the factor `c` every year of age. The result has the shape, dtype and platform of `attained_ages`. Use it for adult mortality; [`gompertz_qx`](gompertz_qx.md) converts it to a one-year probability, and [`makeham_force`](makeham_force.md) adds an age-independent term.

## Parameters

`attained_ages`
: One-dimensional, finite, non-negative ages.

`b`
: Force at age 0, 0 or more.

`c`
: Yearly growth factor, greater than 1.

## Returns

A series of forces, one per age.

## Errors

Throws `gompertz_force: b must be >= 0`, `gompertz_force: c must be > 1 for Gompertz-style age acceleration` and `gompertz_force: attained_ages must be >= 0`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1: forces at four ages

Mortality force rises with age.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(7));
  const pluss::Series ages = pluss::make_series({60.0, 61.0, 62.0, 63.0});
  out.writeln(life::gompertz_force(ages, 0.0001, 1.08).items<double>());
}
```

### Example 2: by hand

The formula `b * c^x`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(7));
  const pluss::Series ages = pluss::make_series({60.0, 61.0, 62.0, 63.0});
  out.writeln(0.0001 * std::pow(1.08, 60.0), 0.0001 * std::pow(1.08, 63.0));
  out.writeln(life::gompertz_force(ages, 0.0001, 1.08).items<double>());
}
```

### Example 3: each year multiplies by c

The ratio of consecutive forces is `c`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series ages = pluss::make_series({60.0, 61.0, 62.0, 63.0});
  const auto mu = life::gompertz_force(ages, 0.0001, 1.08).items<double>();
  out.writeln(mu[1] / mu[0], mu[2] / mu[1], mu[3] / mu[2]);
}
```

### Example 4: the effect of c

A larger growth factor makes old ages far more dangerous.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(5));
  const pluss::Series ages = pluss::make_series({40.0, 60.0, 80.0});
  out.writeln("c = 1.08:", life::gompertz_force(ages, 0.0001, 1.08).items<double>());
  out.writeln("c = 1.10:", life::gompertz_force(ages, 0.0001, 1.10).items<double>());
}
```

### Example 5: the errors

Parameters and ages out of range.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const auto report = [&](const auto &call) {
    try {
      call();
    } catch (const std::exception &e) {
      std::string text(e.what());
      if (const auto cut = text.find("Triggered"); cut != std::string::npos) text.erase(cut);
      while (!text.empty() && text.back() == '\n') text.pop_back();
      out.writeln(text);
    }
  };
  report([&] { (void)life::gompertz_force(pluss::make_series({60.0}), -1.0, 1.08); });
  report([&] { (void)life::gompertz_force(pluss::make_series({60.0}), 0.0001, 1.0); });
  report([&] { (void)life::gompertz_force(pluss::make_series({-1.0}), 0.0001, 1.08); });
}
```

